     <!--#include virtual="/php/suttasidebar.html" --> 

  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="StNp5.9" class="h1">5:9  Todeyya’s Questions</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>One in whom</p>
              <p>no sensualities dwell;</p>
              <p>in whom</p>
              <p>no craving is found;</p>
              <p>who has crossed over perplexity—</p>
              <p class="v1">his emancipation:</p>
              <p class="v1">What is it like?</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                <p>One in whom</p>
                <p>no sensualities dwell;</p>
                <p>in whom</p>
                <p>no craving is found;</p>
                <p>who has crossed over perplexity—</p>
                <p class="v1">his emancipation</p>
                <p class="v1">is not other than that.<span class="fn"><a href="#stnp_note5.9.01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--></p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p class="vspk">Todeyya:</p>
                <p>Is he without desire,</p>
                <p>or desiring?</p>
                <p>Discerning or</p>
                <p>still acquiring discernment?</p>
                <p>Describe the sage to me, Sakyan,</p>
                <p>All-around Eye,</p>
                <p>so that I may recognize</p>
                <p>what he is like.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p class="vspk">The Buddha:</p>
                <p>He’s without desire,</p>
                <p class="v1">not desiring;</p>
                <p>discerning,</p>
                <p>not still acquiring discernment.</p>
                <p>Recognize the sage, Todeyya,</p>
                <p>as having nothing,</p>
                <p>unentangled</p>
                <p class="v1">in sensuality</p>
                <p class="v3">&amp; becoming.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
            <p class="suttaCite">vv. 1088–1091</p><!--end suttaCite-->
            <div class="note">
              <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
              <p id="stnp_note5.9.01">1. Nd IIA: The ending of craving is, in and of itself, emancipation. See <a href="../../SN/SN43.html">SN 43</a>.</p>
            </div><!--end note-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
